### Description

The documentation for useChat ChatHelpers [here](https://sdk.vercel.ai/docs/api-reference/use-chat) says this is how to send dynamic body and headers to the handleSubmit function:

handleSubmit | (e: React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>, options: ChatRequestOptions) => void | Form submission handler that automatically resets the input field and appends a user message.**The chat request options can have a `data` property that you can use to send an extra body object to the API endpoint in addition to the `messages` array**.
-- | -- | --

Which claims `data` should be in ChatRequestOptions, or in the child property within `options`. However, neither of these is correct and this is the only way to pass dynamic body and headers via the api:

```
      await chat.handleSubmit(e, {
        options: {
          body: {
            ...
          },
          headers: {
           ...
          },
        },
```

I believe this is just a documentation fix, but wanted to highlight it here as I've seen other people asking about sending dynamic content (#471).

