### Description

When making a `generateObject` or `streamObject` call with `output: 'no-schema'` and `structuredOuputs: true` on the model settings, the `OpenAIChatLanguageModel` implementation will send a request to OpenAI with the `response_format.json_schema.schema` being undefined. This seems to be due to the fact that the `jsonSchema` returned from the `noSchemaOutputStrategry` is `undefined` (see [here](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/core/generate-object/output-strategy.ts#L47)) which seems correct, but then is passed into `doGenerate` as `mode.schema`, which is ultimately used [here](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/openai/src/openai-chat-language-model.ts#L218).
Passing an `undefined` schema always results in OpenAI responding with a 400, so this execution path will always fail. I believe that this can be resolved by adding a `&& mode.schema !== undefined` to [this line](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/openai/src/openai-chat-language-model.ts#L214), where it seems logical to revert back to using `json_object` should no schema be provided.

### Code example

